-- title:
--   Two q-expansions jointly detect zero after base change to κ
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ be a nonzero natural number and $p$ a prime with $p\nmid N$, and write $\mathbf Z_{(p)}$ for the subring [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt p`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8) of $\mathbf Q$ consisting of the rationals whose denominator is coprime to $p$. Let $\mathcal O^{\infty} =$ `chartAlgInf (N * p) p` be the $\mathbf Z_{(p)}$-subalgebra of the full modular function field of level $Np$ whose elements are those integral over the $\mathbf Z_{(p)}$-subalgebra generated by $j^{-1}$ (the inverse of `jFull`). Let $\kappa$ be a field of characteristic $p$ carrying a $\mathbf Z_{(p)}$-algebra structure. Assume given two ring homomorphisms $\theta_0,\theta_1\colon \mathcal O^{\infty}\to \mathbf F_p(\!(q)\!)$ into the Laurent series over $\mathbf Z/p$ such that each kernel $\ker\theta_i$ is a minimal prime over the ideal $(p)\subseteq\mathcal O^{\infty}$, and such that $\ker\theta_0\neq\ker\theta_1$; and two $\kappa$-algebra homomorphisms $\Theta_0,\Theta_1\colon \kappa\otimes_{\mathbf Z_{(p)}}\mathcal O^{\infty}\to\kappa(\!(q)\!)$ with $\Theta_i(1\otimes b)$ equal to the image of $\theta_i(b)$ under the coefficientwise map induced by $\mathbf Z/p\to\kappa$, for all $b\in\mathcal O^{\infty}$. Then any $x\in\kappa\otimes_{\mathbf Z_{(p)}}\mathcal O^{\infty}$ with $\Theta_0(x)=\Theta_1(x)=0$ is zero.
--
--   This is the statement that the two $q$-expansion maps of the pole chart of the Igusa model of $X_0(Np)$ at a prime $p\nmid N$ remain jointly injective after base change of the special fibre to an arbitrary field $\kappa$ of characteristic $p$. It feeds the count of minimal primes of $\kappa\otimes_{\mathbf Z_{(p)}}\mathcal O^{\infty}$, i.e. the statement that the geometric special fibre of the pole chart has exactly two components.
